      "text": "We are given the function $f(x)$ such that\n\\[f(x) - 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = 4^x.\\]\n\nFirst, let's substitute $x$ with $\\frac{1}{x}$ in the given equation:\n\\[\nf \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) - 2 f(x) = 4^{\\frac{1}{x}}.\n\\]\n\nNow we have a system of two equations:\n1. \\( f(x) - 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = 4^x \\)\n2. \\( f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) - 2 f(x) = 4^{\\frac{1}{x}} \\).\n\nTo eliminate $f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right)$, we can solve for $f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right)$ from the second equation:\n\\[\nf \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = 2 f(x) + 4^{\\frac{1}{x}}.\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute this expression for $f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right)$ into the first equation:\n\\[\nf(x) - 2 \\left( 2 f(x) + 4^{\\frac{1}{x}} \\right) = 4^x.\n\\]\n\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\nf(x) - 4 f(x) - 2 \\cdot 4^{\\frac{1}{x}} = 4^x,\n\\]\n\\[\n-3 f(x) - 2 \\cdot 4^{\\frac{1}{x}} = 4^x.\n\\]\n\nRearrange to solve for $f(x)$:\n\\[\n-3 f(x) = 4^x + 2 \\cdot 4^{\\frac{1}{x}},\n\\]\n\\[\nf(x) = -\\frac{4^x + 2 \\cdot 4^{\\frac{1}{x}}}{3}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find $f(2)$:\n\\[\nf(2) = -\\frac{4^2 + 2 \\cdot 4^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{3} = -\\frac{16 + 2 \\cdot 2}{3} = -\\frac{16 + 4}{3} = -\\frac{20}{3}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of $f(2)$ is \\(\\boxed{-\\frac{20}{3}}\\).\n\nLet's confirm the result using Python code.\n```python\n# Defining the function f(x) based on the derived formula\ndef f(x):\n    return - (4**x + 2 * 4**(1/x)) / 3\n\n# Calculating f(2)\nf_2 = f(2)\nprint(f_2)\n```",
