      "text": "We are given the functional equation:\n\\[ f(x) - 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = 4^x \\]\nWe need to find \\( f(2) \\).\n\nFirst, let's substitute \\( x = 2 \\) into the given equation:\n\\[\nf(2) - 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) = 4^2 = 16\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\nf(2) - 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) = 16 \\tag{1}\n\\]\n\nNext, let's substitute \\( x = \\frac{1}{2} \\) into the given equation:\n\\[\nf \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) - 2 f(2) = 4^{\\frac{1}{2}} = 2\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\nf \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) - 2 f(2) = 2 \\tag{2}\n\\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n1. \\( f(2) - 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) = 16 \\)\n2. \\( f \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) - 2 f(2) = 2 \\)\n\nWe will solve these equations step by step. First, let's solve equation (2) for \\( f \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\):\n\\[\nf \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) = 2 f(2) + 2\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( f \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) = 2 f(2) + 2 \\) into equation (1):\n\\[\nf(2) - 2 (2 f(2) + 2) = 16\n\\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\nf(2) - 4 f(2) - 4 = 16\n\\]\n\\[\n-3 f(2) - 4 = 16\n\\]\n\\[\n-3 f(2) = 20\n\\]\n\\[\nf(2) = -\\frac{20}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( f(2) \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{20}{3}}\n\\]",
